      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To resolve the \"Error 404: Connectivity Lost\" message on your Zenith SmartHub, follow these steps:\n\n1. Restart your router and modem to ensure a fresh connection. This will help clear any temporary issues and allow you to re-establish a stable connection.\n2. Check your internet service provider's (ISP) status to ensure outages in your area are not causing the issue. You can do this by visiting their website or mobile app, or by contacting their customer support via phone or live chat.\n3. Verify that your SmartHub is properly connected to your router using an Ethernet cable. Ensure the cable is securely plugged into both the SmartHub and the router, and that the Ethernet port on the SmartHub is not damaged or malfunctioning.\n4. Check the SmartHub's Wi-Fi settings to ensure it is enabled and set to the correct network. Go to Settings > Wi-Fi and verify that the network is selected and the signal strength is adequate.\n5. If you're using a Wi-Fi connection, try resetting the SmartHub's Wi-Fi adapter by pressing and holding the small pinhole on the back of the device for 10 seconds. This will reset the adapter and may resolve connectivity issues.\n\nBy following these steps, you should",
